# Tests of scripts/e2e/ui/tests/ that are known not to pass yet, one per line:
#
#   <spec file> <test id> <milestone> <the stage that turns it green, and why it is red until then>
#
# The test id is the first word of the test's title. A spec opts in with
# `test.beforeEach(({}, info) => knownRed(info))` (tests/helpers.ts), and Playwright then holds
# the rules the pager's and the issues suite's lists are held to: a listed test that fails is an
# expected failure and the run stays green; a listed test that PASSES is "expected to fail, but
# passed" and the run is red - so the code that turns it green and its line here land in one
# commit. UI_STRICT=1 ignores this file: the release gate's mode, where every listed test fails.
# The milestone is the version whose release needs the test green; once Directory.Build.props'
# floor passes it, the entry is stale and a unit test fails (UiSuiteTests).
